Writes one of ADR-0100's maps of your topic as a record: A domain map, B prerequisite graph, C claim inventory, D evidence mapping, E competency map, F misconception map, G application map, H variability map, I gap audit, J version audit. Each item has a short name, unique in the map, and its text, and cites the stored page passages it rests on by page id and passage number, as fetch and search_pages show them. Code checks each cited passage exists, and that: in C every claim carries its claimType, scope and confidence and cites passages (a claim with no evidence belongs in I as a gap); in D every entry names its sourceTier and cites passages; in B every item gives `after`, naming only items of the map, with no cycle; in J every item gives `checkBy`. A map is written once; change it with change_map.
